The `determinant()` function is a recursive function that calculates the determinant using the cofactor expansion method. It takes two parameters - `mat` which is the matrix and `n` which is the size of the matrix. The base case is when `n` is 1, in which case the function simply returns the single element of the matrix.

The function then iterates over the elements of the first row, calculating the cofactor of each element and recursively calling itself with the cofactor matrix. The determinant is calculated as the sum of the products of the elements of the first row and their respective cofactors, with the sign alternating between positive and negative.

