Here is a recursive solution to flatten a multi-dimensional array in JavaScript:

```javascript
function flattenArray(arr) {
  let result = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    if (Array.isArray(arr[i])) {
      result = result.concat(flattenArray(arr[i]));
    } else {
      result.push(arr[i]);
    }
  }
  return result;
}
```

This function takes in a multi-dimensional array as an argument and returns a flattened array. It uses recursion to check each element of the array to see if it is an array itself or not. If it is an array, it calls the function recursively on that sub-array and concatenates the result to the overall result. If it is not an array, it simply pushes that element to the result array. By doing this recursively, all the elements of the multi-dimensional array are flattened into a single array.

